# Dutch KIS — Core Rules

## The one rule above all others
Every learning feature MUST call `updateWeaknessMap()` at session end.
A feature that doesn't update the weakness map is incomplete.

## Business logic location
- Pure logic → `apps/web/src/lib/` (no Next.js imports)
- API handlers → thin, validate input with Zod, delegate to `lib/`
- React components → UI only, no business logic
- Shared across web + mobile → `packages/` not `apps/`

## Weakness map scoring
Never use raw arithmetic (+3/-2). Always use BKT:
```ts
import { updateSubAxis } from '@/lib/bkt'
await updateSubAxis(userId, 'grammar.separableVerbs', { correct: true, responseTimeMs })
```

## AI calls
All Ollama calls must stream. Never await a full response in an API route:
```ts
import { streamChat } from '@/lib/ollama'
// ✅ stream to client
// ❌ const response = await ollama.complete(...)
```

## Error handling
```ts
// ✅
import { AppError } from '@/lib/errors'
throw new AppError('WEAKNESS_MAP_UPDATE_FAILED', { cause: err })

// ❌
throw new Error('something went wrong')
```
